WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.001
-What an amazing day.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.603
We have a new president,
everybody.

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:06.639
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:08.408
We have the first female,
first black,

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.710
first Asian-American
Vice President.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.379
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.415
I just thought the whole thing
was so great.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:18.851
It was hard not to get emotional
just watching that whole thing.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.252
It was perfectly done.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:24.390
Every performance was top-notch
and everything crushed.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:28.628
Then Amanda Gorman
just comes out of nowhere.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:31.597
I mean, I was like, "What?"
And just crushes --

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:34.667
steals the show from what's
already a great show, I thought.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.469
and I just thought today
was just --

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:39.572
Oh, it was just --
it was a beautiful thing.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.941
But another big deal today --

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:45.511
today is actually
Questlove's 50th birthday.

00:00:45.511 --> 00:00:48.280
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.883
5-0.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:54.720
♪ Da, da da, da dee dee ♪

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.089
Did you think when everyone
was cheering about you

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:59.826
when they opened up the windows
in New York City this morning?

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.794
-I thought it was about me.
-Of course, yeah.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.530
-I thought it was about me.
-Well, we, uh --

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.967
Tariq would like to give you
a gift, a birthday present,

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:10.270
if you don't mind, and would
like to do it right now.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:13.839
-Well, I wanted to give you
a thoughtful gift

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:17.443
because this is a -- you know,
it's a milestone birthday,

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.778
and I know mine
is coming up soon, too.

00:01:19.778 --> 00:01:21.413
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God!

00:01:21.413 --> 00:01:24.017
Oh, my God.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:27.753
-No, so I thought, you know,
what could sort of speak

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:32.858
to your love for music
and, you know, be a nod

00:01:32.858 --> 00:01:36.195
to The Roots and I was thinking
question marks

00:01:36.195 --> 00:01:39.298
and the heart pins
that you wear all the time.

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:42.935
And I said, "If I were gonna
design a logo for you,

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:45.171
what would it be?"
And I was talking

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:49.442
with my sister, Prit,
who is a jewelry designer,

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.244
and she said, "Well, you know,
there's something

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:54.013
that kind of already exists,

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:56.115
you know, that speaks to all
those different things."

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:58.350
And I was -- You know,
I'd already been thinking about

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:02.221
getting a sankofa tattoo.

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:04.457
'Cause I was like, if I'm gonna
get a facial tattoo,

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.725
like, what is it gonna be?"

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.227
So I was gonna get this bird
on my face that is,

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:11.531
like, the sankofa,
which is a word

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:15.067
from the language
in Ghana, West Africa,

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:19.071
that speaks to appreciating
just your roots.

00:02:19.071 --> 00:02:21.574
"Sankofa" means
"Go back and get it."

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:24.210
So, normally,
when you see an emblem

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.712
like the symbol for sankofa,

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:28.580
it's a bird
with his feet facing forward,

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:32.218
and his head is facing its back

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:35.855
and it's holding a delicate egg,
like, in its mouth.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.590
So I'm gonna
get that on my cheek.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:42.027
So I didn't get that for you,
but I realized the other --

00:02:42.027 --> 00:02:45.364
the other --
the other symbol for sankofa

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:48.734
is a stylized heart shape.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:51.337
So I was like,
"Wow. What could I do?"

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:54.941
I designed this heart-shaped
lapel pin for you

00:02:54.941 --> 00:02:56.675
that I want to present you with.

00:02:56.675 --> 00:03:02.548
And it's encrusted in rubies
with a yellow diamond.

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:04.116
Just take that pouch off
the top there.

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:06.085
-Oh, I can't have this part?
Okay.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:08.388
-My birthday was in September,
by the way.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:11.491
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.559
-But you didn't turn 50.
-Yeah.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.061
That's correct.

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.330
-Oh, snap.
-Yeah.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.032
-Wow!
Oh, this is real?

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:20.667
-Yeah.
-Look at that thing.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.202
-Man!
-Well, hold it --

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.770
Hold it like the heart.
-Okay, yes.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:28.140
-There you go.
-Oh, man, thank you.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.543
-And if you look at it on the
back, there's an inscription.

00:03:31.543 --> 00:03:36.616
It says, "From organics
to endgame and beyond.

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:38.284
Brotherly love."

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.552
-Aww.
[ Applause ]

00:03:40.552 --> 00:03:43.689
-Wow!
-Happy birthday.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:45.391
-Thank you.
Man...

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.594
[ Laughter ]
-Aw, come on.

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.829
We never do this,
like, surprise anyone.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:52.264
-I know! I was, like, waiting
for a cake fight or something.

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:53.732
I'm like,
"Oh, this is real! Okay."

00:03:53.732 --> 00:03:55.701
-No.
-Dude, that is so thoughtful.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.503
-Thank you.
-That's amazing, man.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.071
-Yeah.
-I didn't --

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:00.840
You were thinking about
getting a face tattoo?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.009
-Yeah, I'm still gonna get it.
You know, like, the bird

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.745
and he's reaching back
and the egg, you know.

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.713
Probably right around here
somewhere.

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:09.315
I don't want the beard
to cover it up.

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.284
-Yeah. Wow.
-Yeah.

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:14.654
-You should do it too, Jimmy.
-No, I --

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.923
-I mean, you hang out with
Post Malone all the time.

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.290
-I know.
-You guys can --

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.592
-Right now, you know how much
hair and makeup

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.927
I have to go through
to cover my face tattoos?

00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:24.596
So no one knows?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.596 --> 00:04:26.499
Questlove, I wanted
to give you a present, as well,

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:30.502
if I could.
Not a big thing, but it's cool.

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:34.340
But I want --
Can we give it to Quest?

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.643
-Wow. This --
-Not saying.

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:39.679
But my sister's
a jewelry designer, and, uh...

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:42.448
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.283
No, no, no, no, no, no!
No, no.

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:46.519
All right. So the card --
What does the card say?

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.755
-This says 50.
-Okay, now you open the box.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.589
-Okay.

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:58.097
♪♪

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.999
And do you know what it is?

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.368
-No.
-What?

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.670
This is Morris Day's mirror?
-Dude.

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.506
-What?!
-Dude, I called --

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:07.506
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:11.410
-Oh, man, yo --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.847
Dude,
that's Morris Day's mirror.

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:16.416
-Wow.
-From "Purple Rain"?

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:19.018
-Yeah. Dude,
from Morris Day and the Time.

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.153
So I got in touch
with Morris Day.

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:24.290
I got in touch with his --
with his manager, his assistant,

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.991
and I said, "Look," I said,

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:28.661
"I got an idea for Quest
for his birthday."

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.729
I go, "He's turning 50.

00:05:30.729 --> 00:05:32.464
What can I get this guy
who has everything?"

00:05:32.464 --> 00:05:35.501
I go, "He would flip out
to get this."

00:05:35.501 --> 00:05:40.372
So and I said, I go,
"Look, he will cherish it

00:05:40.372 --> 00:05:42.875
more than a museum will."

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:46.478
I go, "Just anything you ever
used in a show or anything,

00:05:46.478 --> 00:05:50.183
he would love it."
And he texted me back.

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:53.352
And he texted me back,
"Ask Jerome."

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:55.020
-Wow.
Wow.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.489
-Because you know Jerome
is like, "Jerome"!

00:05:57.489 --> 00:05:58.858
-Yeah.
-And then Jerome comes out,

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.826
he goes,
"Let me work on something."

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:03.596
Dude, so I had it for, like,
three days, and I'm like,

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:06.466
"This is 50, 'cause you are
looking into your --

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.067
That's what 50 looks like."

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.936
-Guys, I'm speechless, really.
-Wow.

00:06:10.936 --> 00:06:13.272
-Wow. This is amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:16.175
-Look at that.
-Yo, I mean, you know...

00:06:16.175 --> 00:06:19.411
But listen, listen,
since we're talking about gifts,

00:06:19.411 --> 00:06:21.313
are those Christian Dior Jordans
you got on?

00:06:21.313 --> 00:06:24.083
-Yeah, I was gonna say.
-I don't really know.

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:26.085
Are they?
-Wow!

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:28.955
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.956
-Wow.
-Are they good, man?

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:33.159
-I mean, you know...
-Yeah, it's cool.

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:36.629
-Just kind of fun.
-I like J's, too.

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:39.231
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.231 --> 00:06:41.400
-Well, it's
not your birthday yet, you know?

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:45.204
-Well, it was in October.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.204 --> 00:06:47.239
-Anyways, happy birthday,
Questlove!

00:06:47.239 --> 00:06:50.276
Come on.
-Oh, man.

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:52.912
-We love you, buddy.
Here's to many, many, many more.

